 34MG    9BE(36SI,34MGG)               2001YO03                  ENSDF    202609
 34MG  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34MG  H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34MG2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34MG c  2001Yo03, 2002Yo04: a 95-MeV/nucleon, 60-pnA primary beam of {+40}Ar   
 34MG2c  bombarded a 462.5-mg/cm{+2} {+9}Be primary target. A secondary beam of 
 34MG3c  {+36}Si was separated by the RIKEN projectile-fragment separator RIPS  
 34MG4c  and transported to a secondary target of 385.5-mg/cm{+2} {+9}Be at a   
 34MG5c  center-of-target energy of 38 MeV/nucleon. Reaction products from the  
 34MG6c  {+36}Si+{+9}Be fragmentation were detected and identified at forward   
 34MG7c  angles with a parallel-plate avalanche counter (PPAC) and four sets of 
 34MG8c  counter telescopes, each consisting of three silicon detectors and one 
 34MG9c  Si(Li) detector. |g rays emitted from excited fragments were detected  
 34MGAc  using 66 NaI(Tl) detectors. Measured E|g with Doppler correction, I|g, 
 34MGBc  ({+34}Mg)|g-coin, and |g|g-coin. Deduced levels. Also see review       
 34MGCc  articles 2002Sa11 and 2002Mo35.                                        
 34MG c  Advantages of using two-step fragmentations of {+9}Be({+40}Ar,X) and   
 34MG2c  {+9}Be({+36}Si,X): when {+40}Ar is the incident beam, the |g-ray yield 
 34MG3c  for {+34}Mg is low due to a small production cross-section, requiring  
 34MG4c  high beam luminosity and would cause a heavy detection load. In        
 34MG5c  contrast, using {+36}Si, which is closer to {+34}Mg, offers a larger   
 34MG6c  production cross-section, allowing for more intense primary beams      
 34MG7c  (2002Mo35).                                                            
 34MG cG E$From 2001Yo03.                                                       
 34MG cL E$From E|g data of 2001Yo03. The energies of the first 4+ level and the
 34MG2cL first 2+ level yield an R{-4/2}=3.2, which is very close to 10/3       
 34MG3cL expected for a rigid rotor and {+34}Mg might be a nucleus with         
 34MG4cL well-developed quadrupole deformation (2001Yo03).                      
 34MG cL J$Assigned based on fragmentation reaction systematics of magnesium    
 34MG2cL isotopes (2001Yo03).                                                   
